From: K230 SDK <dev@canaan-creative.com>
Date: Thu, 17 Jul 2026 00:00:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] riscv: dts: canaan: configure GPIO66 as USB Host power enable

GPIO66 (IO66, gpio1_ports_b pin 2) is the USB Host power enable pin.
The external circuit pulls this pin up to 5V via a resistor.

The PMU IOMUX default enables internal pull-down, which fights the
external pull-up. This patch:

1. Adds pmu_usb_host_pwr_pin pinctrl node for IO66:
   - function = "alt1" (GPIO mode)
   - bias-disable (disable internal pull-down)
2. Adds gpio-hog on gpio1_ports_b to drive output-high at boot.

Note: IO66 is NOT in pmu_rgb_led_pins because that group inherits
the default pull-down needed by active-low RGB LEDs.

Signed-off-by: K230 SDK <dev@canaan-creative.com>
---
 arch/riscv/boot/dts/canaan/k230-canmv-v3.dts     | 18 ++++++++++++++++++
 arch/riscv/boot/dts/canaan/k230-canmv-v3-lcd.dts | 18 ++++++++++++++++++
 2 files changed, 36 insertions(+)

--- a/arch/riscv/boot/dts/canaan/k230-canmv-v3.dts
+++ b/arch/riscv/boot/dts/canaan/k230-canmv-v3.dts
@@ -157,3 +157,21 @@
 	pmu_rgb_led_pins: pmu_rgb_led_pins {
 		pins = K230_IO64, K230_IO65;
 		function = "alt1";
+	};
+};
+
+&pmuiomux {
+	pmu_usb_host_pwr_pin: pmu_usb_host_pwr_pin {
+		pins = K230_IO66;
+		function = "alt1";
+		bias-disable;
+	};
+};
+&gpio1_ports_b {
+	gpio66_hog: gpio66-hog {
+		gpio-hog;
+		gpios = <2 GPIO_ACTIVE_HIGH>;
+		output-high;
+		line-name = "usb-host-pwr";
+	};
+};
--- a/arch/riscv/boot/dts/canaan/k230-canmv-v3-lcd.dts
+++ b/arch/riscv/boot/dts/canaan/k230-canmv-v3-lcd.dts
@@ -125,3 +125,21 @@
 	pmu_rgb_led_pins: pmu_rgb_led_pins {
 		pins = K230_IO64, K230_IO65;
 		function = "alt1";
+	};
+};
+
+&pmuiomux {
+	pmu_usb_host_pwr_pin: pmu_usb_host_pwr_pin {
+		pins = K230_IO66;
+		function = "alt1";
+		bias-disable;
+	};
+};
+&gpio1_ports_b {
+	gpio66_hog: gpio66-hog {
+		gpio-hog;
+		gpios = <2 GPIO_ACTIVE_HIGH>;
+		output-high;
+		line-name = "usb-host-pwr";
+	};
+};
